WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.830
A Torah scroll is written by
hand, by a trained scribe,

2
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:06.010
with a quill on parchment.

3
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:11.450
One wrong or missing letter, and the scroll
cannot be used until it is corrected.

4
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:16.900
And if a scroll is dropped, in many
communities everyone who saw it will fast.

5
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.980
So why might a congregation
fast over a dropped scroll?

6
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.980
And what else guides
Jewish life besides it?

7
00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:28.960
In this mission, you'll unpack the three
parts of the Jewish Bible, the Tenakh.

8
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.800
Then you'll follow a chain of teaching
that starts with the Torah and reaches

9
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.730
the Mishnah, around 200 CE.

10
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.960
Your mission: find out why a
dropped scroll matters so much,

11
00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.950
and what else guides Jewish life.
